{"resourceIdentifier":"1403","resourceName":"The Paraguay Forest Conservation Project – Reduction of GHG Emissions from Deforestation and Forest Degradation in the Parana Atlantic Ecosystem – Forest Protection in the La Amistad Community, San Rafael","description":"The project goal is to conserve the natural qualities, including the stored carbon, of the Atlantic Forest in Eastern Paraguay. This has extremely high conservation value and is highly threatened. The fate is of national and international concern. The strategy is to make payments for ecosystem services for forest conservation to small holders,living within small holder communities that have been resettled on land redistributed under theParaguayan Agrarian Reform Programme within the remnants of the Atlantic Forest within the project boundary in Eastern Paraguay. These communities have the legal right to clear the forest. The project is thus expected to generate GHG emission reductions through reducing emissions from deforestation. Based on the initial project instances annual average GHG emission reductions are estimated tobe 1,265 tC02e while total GHG emission reductions are estimated to be 25,306 tC02e.PUBLIC COMMENT PERIOD:This project was open for public comment from 03 December 2019 - 02 January 2020. Documents up for comment at this time: 1. CCB_MONT_REP_ENG_DRAFT_1403_31OCT2013_30OCT20172. CCB_MONT_REP_SUM_ESP_1403_31OCT2013_30OCT2017","location":{"latitude":-26.923259,"longitude":-55.971380},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1403"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Itapua"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Swire Pacific Offshore Operations (Pte) Ltd. (SPO)"},{"type":"string","value":"Singapore, Singapore"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},